            <ArticleTitle>Selecting a treatment option in subungual haematoma management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>59, 61, 63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A subungual haematoma is a collection of blood beneath a finger or toe nail. It is often caused by a crush injury (Purcell, 2003) such as shutting a finger in a door or other types of trauma. Heim et al (2000) note that these haematomas can also be caused by repetitive trauma in athletes such as runners and dancers.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
